WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.120
There are several types of IPv6 addresses
to know about for the exam and understanding

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.390
what types of addresses you have and can work
with when using IPv6.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.990
I have run ipconfig on this device, and right
away, I see two types of IPv6 addresses.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:19.050
The one that starts with 2601 is a global
unicast address.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.330
Global unicast addresses usually start with
either a 2 or a 3.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.800
A global unicast address in IPv6 is equivalent
to a public IPv4 address.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:34.629
A unique local IPv6 address starts with an
FC or an FD.

00:00:34.629 --> 00:00:39.589
Those are public IPv6 addresses as well, but
they are only routable within a single domain.

00:00:39.589 --> 00:00:43.750
The other common IPv6 address we see is a
link-local address.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.280
A link-local IPv6 address starts with FE80.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.870
These are fairly equivalent to a private IPv4
address in that these addresses can communicate

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.730
with other devices on a local network.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:02.160
Still, technically these addresses are most
similar to the IPv4 APIPA addresses, which

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.790
start with 169.254.

